{"id": "10783774-47bd-4b65-956d-91202c2ab7ff", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T18:44:51.579318", "source": "user", "parent_id": "79806084-be03-4167-945c-bc2128096cb1", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"This is a design-only experiment design task. Please do NOT execute simulations or heavy compute; produce a written experiment design. Begin with an inspection step and a proposed approach, then stop and wait for my review before producing the full design. Specifically, I need from you now (initial_inspection only): (1) Workspace inspection: list the contents of /workspace (top-level tree, two levels deep). Note any existing code, data, configs, README, or notes about the forward simulation model, the MD ground-truth dataset for tetrapeptides, or prior TICA/coordinate featurization. Report only what is actually present; do not invent files. (2) Evidence inventory: for each topic in the fixed requirements (tetrapeptides all-atom MD system; backbone torsion angles; sidechain torsion angles) and the question's reference to top TICA components, quote or summarize the relevant verbatim text from any document you found. If nothing is present in the repo, say so explicitly. (3) Proposed approach: a concise outline of (a) how to define the two distributions to be compared (sampled trajectories vs. ground-truth MD trajectories, with matching splits/time origins); (b) the chosen collective variables (backbone phi/psi/omega per residue where applicable, sidechain chi angles per residue, and TICA components built from these torsions — state how TICA is fit only on training data, lag choice, number of components, and how projection is applied); (c) distributional similarity metrics per CV (e.g., 1D marginal KDE/weighted histogram with JS or Wasserstein distance, possibly 2D Ramachandran/free-energy surfaces with JS, plus a multivariate summary on top TICA coordinates); (d) controls and confounding safeguards (same timestep, same temperature/conformation-equivalent frames, identical featurization pipeline, confidence intervals via block/bootstrap, random seeds fixed, sample-size justification); (e) feasibility within a CPU-only, network-disabled bubblewrap compute budget with no preinstalled deps. (4) Assumptions and uncertainties: list every assumption you are making that is not directly supported by the inspected inputs — e.g., number/identity of residues in the tetrapeptides, identity of the forward model, dataset format, available compute budget, library availability. (5) Open clarifications: a short list of questions you would need answered before producing the final design (sources of ground truth, sources of samples, whether Boltzmann reweighting/JSD on weights or unweighted samples is expected, reporting format). Do not produce the full experiment design yet. Do not run code. Return ONLY the inspection report, evidence quotes, proposed approach, assumptions, and open clarifications.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"Do the sampled trajectories from the forward simulation model exhibit distributional similarity to ground-truth MD trajectories across key collective variables, such as backbone torsions, sidechain torsions, and top TICA components?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 24, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [\"neurips2024/93022/0:setup_2\", \"neurips2024/93022/0:setup_13\", \"neurips2024/93022/0:setup_14\"], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 1}
