\\n- `env` exposes only `PWD=/workspace`; no dataset paths or repo roots\\n- GPU: per task context, none; CPU affinity: 24\\n\\n## 2) Evidence inventory (verbatim from `/workspace/task.json`)\\n\\nThe only document in the repo is `task.json`. Treating its two semantic fields as the evidence:\\n\\n- Question (verbatim):\\n  > \\\"Do the sampled trajectories from the forward simulation model exhibit distributional similarity to ground-truth MD trajectories across key collective variables, such as backbone torsions, sidechain torsions, and top TICA components?\\\"\\n\\n- Context (verbatim):\\n  > \\\"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\\\"\\n\\n- Documents map (verbatim — note this is an inline string, not an on-disk file):\\n  > `\\\"documents\\\": { \\\"track.md\\\": \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\" }`\\n\\nTopic-by-topic evidence status:\\n\\n| Required topic | Repository evidence |\\n|---|---|\\n| Tetrapeptides all-atom MD system | None. No sequence, residue identity, force field, box, integrator, temperature, or trajectory files are present anywhere in the repo. |\\n| Backbone torsion angles (φ/ψ/ω) | None. No script, topology, or featurization code is present. No atom-typing convention is documented. |\\n| Sidechain torsion angles (χ) | None. No residue identities → cannot enumerate χ; no code present. |\\n| Top TICA components / TICA delay convention | None. No prior model. No lag, number-of-components, or library choice documented. |\\n\\nThe only source-supported constraints are the question sentence (which names the three CV families and the \\\"top TICA components\\\" framing) and the inline document note saying the task is design-only and that \\\"repositories and compute are not required\\\". No ground-truth file paths, file formats, sample counts, or library constraints are documented in the repo.\\n\\n## 3) Proposed approach (sketch — full design withheld pending your approval)\\n\\n### (a) Two distributions to compare\\n- **Ground-truth MD trajectories** (reference): all-atom MD ensemble for a single tetrapeptide at fixed (T, P), drawn from a single equilibrium seed-per-replica after discarding an equilibration prefix t_eq.\\n- **Sampled trajectories** (test): independent draws from the forward simulation model for the **same** sequence, ideally with the same number of replicas and the same physical timestep / saved-frame stride; equilibration (if any generative warm-up) handled with a matched burn-in.\\n- **Time-origin / split handling:**\\n  - Replica-split: hold out a fraction (e.g., 2/3 for fit, 1/3 for evaluation) at the **replica level** (so TICA is fit on trajectories it never sees projected).\\n  - Within-trajectory discard: first t_eq discarded; frames decorrelated by stride of Δ = ⌈τ_int / dt_save⌉ to avoid leakage of autocorrelation into CI estimates.\\n  - Both distributions are compared on identical per-frame featurizations (see (b)).\\n\\n### (b) Collective variables and TICA pipeline\\n- **Featurization (identical for both sets):**\\n  - Backbone: per-residue φ_i, ψ_i, ω_i for i = 1..N_res (with N_res = 4 for a tetrapeptide; ω defined only at interior peptide bonds if applicable; terminal bonds handled consistently).\\n  - Sidechain: per-residue χ1_i, χ2_i, … as defined by the residue identity (length depends on residue type). Each torsion wrapped to (−π, π].\\n  - Periodic encoding: each torsion fed to TICA as (sin θ, cos θ) per angle to enforce circular topology; raw angles retained for marginals.\\n- **TICA training:**\\n  - Fit **only** on the ground-truth training split. Lag τ chosen to lie in a reasonable kinetic regime (typical reference: τ ≈ 1–10 ps; exact value to be set from autocorrelation of a fast variable like ψ, after we know dt). Number of components: keep components whose eigenvalues exceed a threshold (e.g., > 1/4 of the leading component, or use a kinetic-map-style ≥ 0.5 of the first eigenvalue); default k ≈ 5–10 subject to spectral-gap inspection.\\n  - Projection: apply the fitted TICA map (mean-centered, with the same sin/cos basis) to the held-out frames of both distributions; otherwise the model never sees the test set.\\n\\n### (c) Distributional-similarity metrics per CV\\n- **1D marginals:** For each φ_i, ψ_i, ω_i, χj_i, and top-k TICA scores — KDE on a uniform grid (e.g., 50 bins for torsions, 36 for wrap-safe circular KDE; bandwidth by Silverman / Scott) and a periodic-aware weighted histogram. Metrics: Jensen–Shannon divergence (bits), 1-Wasserstein (circular W1 for torsions), both reported.\\n- **2D surfaces:** (φ_i, ψ_i) per residue (Ramachandran), (ψ_i, χ1_i), and (TICA-1, TICA-2). 2D histograms (e.g., 36×36), JSD on normalized counts.\\n- **Multivariate summary:** On top-k TICA components, energy distance or unbiased MMD with bootstrap CIs; optionally Wasserstein-2 after projecting onto the first two ICs (useful for free-energy-style plots F = −kT log p).\\n- **Effect-size calibration:** report JSD and W1 side by side with bootstrap 95% CIs (block bootstrap on replica-level blocks to respect autocorrelation).\\n\\n### (d) Controls and confounding safeguards\\n- Same featurization pipeline (single function, single version) for both sets; no per-set re-tuning.\\n- Same dt and temperature between ground-truth and (reported) sample-generation conditions; document any mismatch as a caveat rather than silently reweighting.\\n- TICA fit on ground-truth training split only — never on the generative samples — to avoid target leakage.\\n- Fixed integer seeds for KDE bandwidth selection, bootstrap resampling, and any random pair selection in the multivariate tests.\\n- Sample-size justification: report the effective sample size n_eff = n_frames·Δ/τ_int per distribution and a power note (JSD precision ≈ N_bins / n_eff for KDE-based metrics).\\n- Family-wise correction: Benjamini–Hochberg FDR across the family of CV-level tests, since we are running dozens of marginals.\\n\\n### (e) Feasibility inside this bubblewrap (CPU-only, no network, no preinstalled deps)\\n- **Hard constraint:** none of NumPy, SciPy, pandas, mdtraj, PyEMMA, scikit-learn, or matplotlib are importable; pip is not on PATH; network is off → cannot pip-install.\\n- **Consequence:** the experiment as designed above cannot be *executed* in this exact environment without vendored wheels or a prebuilt environment. The task document explicitly says \\\"repositories and compute are not required\\\" and \\\"Do not claim that an experiment was run\\\", so the correct deliverable is the design — not a run. Where I do give example implementations in the full design, I will write them against a standard library (`pyemma.coordinates`, `mdtraj.compute_dihedrals`, `deeptime`) and call out that an actual execution needs those deps present.\\n- **CPU budget reality check (for sizing only):** on 24 CPUs, TICA on ≤ ~200k frames of (sin, cos)-encoded torsions (≈ 8–24 of them) is minutes-to-tens-of-minutes; KDE / 2D histograms on millions of frames is minutes. So the *design's compute footprint* is reasonable, even though the *current bubble* cannot host it.\\n\\n## 4) Assumptions (not supported by inspected inputs)\\n\\n1. The tetrapeptide is a single-sequence object (so sidechain torsions are well-defined for **some** non-alanine residue, since alanine has no χ); this is not stated. If the system is pure alanine, the sidechain-torsion comparison collapses to a vacuous statement and should be re-scoped.\\n2. The forward simulation model produces **unweighted** configurations (otherwise JSD on counts is a comparison of weighted densities, which needs Boltzmann reweighting or kBT corrections).\\n3. Both sources share the same physical (T, P, force field, residue protonation, termini capping) — otherwise dihedral distributions will differ for uninteresting thermodynamic reasons.\\n4. Frame count and stride are matched or can be matched; equil/discard conventions are alignable between ground truth and the forward model.\\n5. TICA lag τ is in a regime where the slowest captured process is physically meaningful — we will need to know dt_save to choose τ sensibly.\\n6. Topology files (or atom indices for dihedrals) are externally available; if not, an all-atom MD topology will need to be reconstructed from sequence.\\n7. For reporting, \\\"top TICA components\\\" means top-k = 2–4 by eigenvalue, not a fixed single component.\\n8. The intended output is a per-CV similarity table with CIs and qualitative 2D-surface plots, not a single global statistic.\\n9. Bootstrap must be block (replica-level) to respect autocorrelation of both ensembles independently.\\n\\n## 5) Open clarifications (needed before final design)\\n\\n1. **Sequence / system identity.** Exactly which tetrapeptide(s)? Caps (Ace/NMe vs. zwitterion vs. charged termini)? Force field and water model? Are we evaluating one sequence or a panel?\\n2. **Source and format of ground truth.** File format(s), total simulation length per replica, number of replicas, temperature(s), saved stride, equilibration protocol, availability of a topology file.\\n3. **Source and format of sampled trajectories.** Which forward model exactly (diffusion / flow / MCMC / mix)? How many independent trajectories, what length, what stride, any generation-time burn-in?\\n4. **Sample weighting.** Are the model outputs unweighted configurations or do they carry per-frame weights (e.g., from a reweighting or importance-sampling step)? If weights exist, should similarity be computed on weighted histograms?\\n5. **What \\\"distribution\\\" means.** Equilibrium configuration distribution p(x) only, or also a kinetic-lag claim (autocorrelation of TICA components at τ)? The question is ambiguous; \\\"top TICA components\\\" hints at the kinetic view, but the body asks about distributional similarity on those CVs.\\n6. **Statistical strictness.** What FDR/α level is expected across the many per-CV tests? Should we report a single global \\\"passes / fails\\\" or a per-CV table?\\n7. **TICA hyperparameter freedom.** May I pick τ and k from a documented protocol (autocorrelation of a fast variable, plus spectral-gap threshold), or are τ and k externally mandated?\\n8. **Library and environment.** For the full-design write-up, may I specify standard libs (mdtraj, PyEMMA, deeptime, scipy) with the explicit caveat that the current bubblewrap is empty and execution is out of scope? Or should I constrain the design to pure stdlib (in which case TICA reduces to a manual covariance-eigenproblem implementation and torsion featurization is hand-rolled over PDB atom indices)?\\n9. **Output deliverables.** Markdown report only, or also CSV of per-CV JSD/W1 and a few Ramachandran / TICA-1/2 density plots (PNG)? Plots are not executable in this bubble without matplotlib.\\n10. **What is \\\"out of scope / not required to demonstrate\\\".** The inline track string says repos and compute are not required — I will treat that as license not to fabricate runs; please confirm it also means I do not need to specify outside-bubble wrap-up steps (vendoring wheels, container build, etc.).\\n\\n---\\nStopping here per your instruction. No full design, no simulations, no fabricated runs. Awaiting your review/approval (and answers to the open clarifications above where possible) before I produce the complete experiment design in `stage=result`.\\n\",\"evidence\":\"Direct read of `/workspace/task.json` (the only file in the entire workspace): {\\\"question\\\":\\\"Do the sampled trajectories from the forward simulation model exhibit distributional similarity to ground-truth MD trajectories across key collective variables, such as backbone torsions, sidechain torsions, and top TICA components?\\\",\\\"context\\\":\\\"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\\\",\\\"documents\\\":{\\\"track.md\\\":\\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\"}}. Additional evidence confirming emptiness: `find /workspace -type f` returns only `/workspace/task.json`; `ls /workspace/.*` returns nothing; `find / -maxdepth 4 -type f \\\\( -name track.md -o -name *tetrapeptide* -o -name *alanine* -o -name *neurips2024* \\\\)` returns no project-relevant matches. Preinstalled-packages probe via `importlib.util.find_spec` reports numpy/scipy/pandas/torch/mdtraj/pyemma/sklearn/matplotlib as MISSING; `which` not in PATH; `env | grep -iE data|workspace|repo|task` shows only `PWD=/workspace`.\",\"assumptions\":\"See section 4 of the plan answer: sequence identity, sample weighting, matched thermodynamic conditions, frame-count alignment, TICA lag regime, topology availability, k in top-k TICA, output format, and block-bootstrap level are all assumptions because the repo provides no on-disk evidence for them.\",\"uncertainties\":\"See section 5 of the plan answer: open clarifications on sequence/caps/force field, file formats for both ground truth and model samples, weighted vs. unweighted samples, kinetic vs. configurational similarity interpretation, FDR level, τ/k authority, library/environment constraints for the write-up, output deliverables, and scope of \\\"compute not required\\\".\"}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-e59a5fd6-78d2-45bd-8e57-19b33c6e8797", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 14}
