nsemble for a single tetrapeptide at fixed (T, P), drawn from independent replicas after discarding an equilibration prefix t_eq.\\n- Sampled trajectories (test): independent draws from the forward simulation model for the same sequence, ideally the same number of replicas and the same physical timestep / saved-frame stride; any generative warm-up handled with a matched burn-in.\\n- Time-origin / split handling:\\n  - Replica-split: hold out a fraction (e.g., 2/3 fit, 1/3 evaluation) at the replica level, so TICA is fit on trajectories it never sees projected.\\n  - Within-trajectory discard: first t_eq discarded; frames decorrelated by stride \\u0394 = \\u2308\\u03c4_int / dt_save\\u2309 to avoid autocorrelation leakage into CI estimates.\\n  - Both distributions are compared on identical per-frame featurizations.\\n\\n### (b) Collective variables and TICA pipeline\\n- Featurization (identical for both sets):\\n  - Backbone: per-residue \\u03c6_i, \\u03c8_i, \\u03c9_i for i = 1..N_res with N_res = 4 for a tetrapeptide; \\u03c9 defined only at interior peptide bonds; terminal bonds handled consistently or omitted.\\n  - Sidechain: per-residue \\u03c71_i, \\u03c72_i, ... as defined by residue identity (length depends on residue type). Each torsion wrapped to (\\u2212\\u03c0, \\u03c0].\\n  - Periodic encoding: each torsion fed to TICA as (sin \\u03b8, cos \\u03b8) per angle to enforce circular topology; raw angles retained for marginals and Ramachandran surfaces.\\n- TICA training:\\n  - Fit only on the ground-truth training split. Lag \\u03c4 in a reasonable kinetic regime (typical 1\\u201310 ps; exact value set from autocorrelation of a fast variable like \\u03c8 once dt_save is known). Number of components by spectral gap (e.g., eigenvalues \\u2265 0.5 of the leading one, or > 1/4 of the leading); default k \\u2248 5\\u201310 subject to inspection.\\n  - Projection: apply the fitted TICA map (mean-centered, same sin/cos basis) to held-out frames of both distributio