s, mdtraj, PyEMMA, scikit-learn, matplotlib are all missing; pip is not on PATH; network is off, so pip-install is impossible.\\n- Consequence: the experiment as designed above cannot be executed in this exact environment without vendored wheels or a prebuilt environment. The task document explicitly says \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required\\\" and \\\"Do not claim that an experiment was run\\\", so the correct deliverable is the design \\u2014 not a run. Where the full design specifies example implementation, it will be against standard libraries (mdtraj, PyEMMA, deeptime) with a clear note that execution requires those deps.\\n- CPU sizing sanity check: on 24 CPUs, TICA on \\u2264 ~200k frames of (sin, cos)-encoded torsions (\\u2248 8\\u201324 features) is minutes-to-tens-of-minutes; KDE / 2D histograms on millions of frames is minutes. The design's compute footprint is reasonable; the bubble itself just cannot host it.\\n\\nStopping here per your instruction. No full design, no simulations, no fabricated runs. Awaiting your review and answers to the open clarifications before I produce the complete experiment design in `stage=result`.\\n\", \"evidence\": \"Direct read of `/workspace/task.json` (the only file in the entire workspace): {\\\"question\\\":\\\"Do the sampled trajectories from the forward simulation model exhibit distributional similarity to ground-truth MD trajectories across key collective variables, such as backbone torsions, sidechain torsions, and top TICA components?\\\",\\\"context\\\":\\\"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\\\",\\\"documents\\\":{\\\"track.md\\\":\\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\"}}. Additional evidence confirming emptiness: `find /workspace -type f` returns only `/workspace/task.json`; `ls /workspace/.*` returns nothing; `find / -maxdepth 4 -type 