divided by ln(2)) on a 50-bin 1D grid; 2D JSD on 36x36 grids; circular 1-Wasserstein in radians for torsion CVs only.\", \"Bh FDR is applied independently within three pre-defined families (A_torsions_1d, B_surfaces_2d, C_energy_distance), at q = 0.05, using statsmodels multipletests.\", \"Informational TICA autocorrelation times (per-frame-weighted) are reported per ensemble and never used as a pass/fail criterion.\", \"Plus-args versions (mdtraj >= 1.9, pyemma >= 2.5 or deeptime >= 0.4, scipy >= 1.10, scikit-learn >= 1.2, etc.) are illustrative; actual versions are pinned in requirements.txt at run time.\", \"The present bubblewrap cannot install or import these libraries; this Markdown document is the deliverable and no execution is performed.\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"Exact identity of the canonical tetrapeptide sequence, force field, water treatment are not source-supported in the repo; protocol does not depend on these choices per the binding defaults (panel-config-driven).\", \"Exact file format / path / version history of MD and forward-model trajectories are not in the repo; logged in config.yaml at run time.\", \"Whether temperature-rescaling / Boltzmann reweighting should be applied if MD and Model differ in reported T is not pre-decided; design currently logs the mismatch as a flagged control without applying any reweighting (binding \\u00a72.4).\", \"Whether the canonical panel is actually Ace-Ala4-NMe or a different sequence with chi-bearing residues is open; the protocol works regardless.\", \"Whether to use PyEMMA or deeptime at run time depends on which is available; both are supported and the choice is recorded in config.yaml.\", \"Future tweaks to the lag ladder, FDR q, or block-bootstrap replicate count B can be made by editing config.yaml without changing the protocol.\"]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-2c9b956f-b23a-4366-9c74-f4d4ddf15d94", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 21}
